# The build context for the multi-stage Dockerfile at the repository root.
#
# The list is short on purpose. Anything excluded here cannot reach the builder,
# and anything that reaches the *builder* still cannot reach the runtime image,
# which copies only `dist/` and the nginx fragments. The entries below are the
# ones that would either break the build or bloat every layer.

# Installed dependencies. The builder reinstalls them from pnpm-lock.yaml, and a
# host's `node_modules` copied in would be the wrong platform's binaries (this
# repository is developed on macOS) and would silently defeat the point of
# `--frozen-lockfile`.
node_modules
.pnpm-store

# Build output. Built inside the image; a stale `dist/` copied in alongside it
# could be what the runtime stage ends up serving.
dist
storybook-static

# Test output
coverage

# Environment files. The browser-visible Supabase values arrive as build
# arguments (see the Dockerfile); a `.env` copied in would shadow them, and a
# populated one would put real values into a layer.
.env
.env.*

# Git metadata: not needed to build, and it changes on every commit for no
# benefit. Husky is disabled during the image install for the same reason.
.git
.gitignore

# CI configuration is not part of the artefact.
.github

# A design reference kept at the repository root. It is not part of this app,
# is not built or shipped, and is not imported by anything — it is here to be
# read. No reason to copy it into a build context.
source.tsx

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
*.log
